deos/times-now/shows\">Shows</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/times-now/newshour\">Newshour</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/times-now/india-upfront\">India Upfront</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/times-now/nation-wants-to-know\">Nation Wants To Know</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/times-now/frankly-speaking\">Frankly Speaking</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/times-now/specials\">Specials</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/gadgets\">Digit</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/viral-videos\">Viral Video</a></li><li><a href=\"/videos/times-now/elections\">Elections</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"/education\">Education</a></li><li><a href=\"/technology-science\">Tech</a></li><li><a href=\"/weather\">Weather</a></li><li><a href=\"/web-stories\">Web Stories</a></li><li><a href=\"/elections\">Elections</a></li><li><a href=\"/topic/leaders-of-tomorrow\">LOT</a></li><li><a href=\"/health\">Health</a></li><li><a href=\"/auto\">Auto</a><ul><li><a href=\"/auto/car-news\">Car News</a></li><li><a href=\"/auto/bike-news\">Bike News</a></li><li><a href=\"/auto/electric-vehicles\">Electric Vehicles</a></li><li><a href=\"/auto/features\">Features</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"/viral\">Viral</a></li><li><a href=\"/opinion\">Opinion</a><ul><li><a href=\"/opinion/world\">World</a></li><li><a href=\"/opinion/india\">India</a></li></ul></li><li><a href=\"/spiritual\">Spirituality</a></li><li><a href=\"/astrology\">Astrology</a></li><li><a href=\"/photos\">Photos</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></header><div class=\"\"><div class=\"layout-section\"><div class=\"Renderer_layoutrow__H5Vjk Renderer_fullwidth__PrOrS  \"><div class=\"layout-col\"><main id=\"article_main\" data-llm=\"true\"><div class=\"ContainerBox_container__i9uR9  \"><div class=\"ArticleTop_articleTop__MFbq3\"><a class=\"ArticleTop_category__gjY9S\" href=\"#\">Spotlight</a><h1>10 Indoor Plants That Thrive During Monsoon</h1><div class=\"\"><ul><li><span>Authored by<!-- -->: <a href=\"https://www.timesnownews.com/author/kirti-chauhan-479251617\">Kirti Chauhan</a></span></li><li>Updated: Aug 25, 2026, 16:39 IST</li></ul></div><h2>Monsoon is a great time to add greenery to your indoor spaces, thanks to the season’s high humidity. Discover 10 indoor plants that thrive during monsoon and are easy to maintain at home. From Snake Plant and Money Plant to Peace Lily and Boston Fern, these plants can brighten your interiors. Learn simple monsoon indoor plant care tips to keep your plants healthy and fresh.</h2></div><div class=\"ArticleShow_articleRow__Bqz2c\" style=\"display:flex;margin-top:18px\"><div class=\"ArticleShow_lhs__PS2wz\" style=\"flex:1 1 0%;min-width:0;margin-right:20px\"><div class=\"CoverImage_articleImg__sESKo null\"><img src=\"https://images.timesnownews.com/thumb/msid-155983447,thumbsize-1362292,width-1280,height-720,resizemode-75/155983447.jpg\" data-src=\"https://images.timesnownews.com/thumb/msid-155983447,thumbsize-1362292,width-1280,height-720,resizemode-75/155983447.jpg\" alt=\"10 Indoor Plants That Thrive During Monsoon\" decoding=\"async\" fetchPriority=\"high\" loading=\"eager\" data-width=\"1280\" data-height=\"720\" style=\"display:block;object-fit:cover;object-position:center;transition:opacity 0.4s ease;opacity:1;overflow:hidden\" layout=\"fixed\"/><p>10 Indoor Plants That Thrive During Monsoon</p></div><div class=\"SocialShare_followrow__SHotd\"><div class=\"SocialShare_followlink__fcLEO\"><a aria-label=\"googlenews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://profile.google.com/cp/CgkvbS8wZ3NmeHE\"><img src=\"/nimg/assets/icons/svg/googleNewsIconNew.svg\" alt=\"GoogleNewsIcon\"/>follow us</a><a aria-label=\"whtsapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029Va7R81560eBdf7e61g0T\"><svg class=\"SvgIcon_icon-md__09S9E\"><use xlink:href=\"/nimg/assets/icons/svg/sprite-global.svg?version=4#DarkWhatsAppIcon\"></use></svg>follow us</a></div><a class=\"SocialShare_googlesource__sveyC\" href=\"https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=times now\" aria-label=\"Set as preferred source on Google News\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://images.timesnownews.com/photo/152643139.cms\" alt=\"google\"/></a></div><article id=\"mgIDReadMore\" class=\"\" data-llm=\"true\"><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>The monsoon season brings cooler temperatures and higher humidity, creating favourable conditions for several indoor plants. However, excess moisture and poor air circulation can also lead to root rot, fungal growth and pest problems. Choosing the right plants can help you maintain a fresh and green indoor space without demanding too much care.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>If you are looking for indoor plants for monsoon, here are 10 options that can grow well in humid conditions with proper care.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>1. Snake Plant</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>The Snake Plant is one of the easiest indoor plants to grow during the monsoon. It can tolerate different light conditions and does not require frequent watering. Since the soil tends to remain moist for longer during rainy weather, avoid watering it unless the top layer of soil feels dry.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Keep the plant in a well-drained pot and avoid waterlogging.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>2. Money Plant</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Money Plant is a popular choice for Indian homes because it is easy to maintain and can grow in both soil and water. It can thrive in bright, indirect sunlight and generally adapts well to humid conditions.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Place it near a window where it receives indirect light and maintains good air circulation.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>3. Spider Plant</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>The Spider Plant is another low-maintenance indoor plant suitable for the monsoon season. Its long, arching leaves can add a refreshing touch to living rooms, bedrooms and workspaces.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Water only when the soil begins to dry and make sure the pot has drainage holes.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>4. Peace Lily</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Peace Lily is known for its attractive green leaves and white flowers. It prefers humid surroundings, making the monsoon season suitable for its growth. However, excess water can damage its roots.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Keep it in bright, indirect light and avoid allowing water to collect in the pot or tray.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>5. Boston Fern</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Boston Fern loves humidity and can benefit from the naturally moist air during the monsoon. Its dense green foliage makes it a good choice for adding greenery to indoor spaces.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Keep the soil lightly moist but not soggy. Place the plant in indirect sunlight with good ventilation.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>6. Areca Palm</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Areca Palm can bring a tropical feel to your home and generally does well in warm, humid conditions. It needs bright, indirect light and regular monitoring of soil moisture.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: During the monsoon, reduce watering if the soil remains damp for several days.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>7. ZZ Plant</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>The ZZ Plant is highly tolerant and is suitable for people who prefer low-maintenance greenery. It can survive in low to moderate indirect light and does not need frequent watering.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Allow the soil to dry between waterings, especially during periods of high humidity.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>8. Rubber Plant</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Rubber Plant has broad, glossy leaves that can make an indoor space look more vibrant. It prefers bright, indirect sunlight and moderate watering.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Wipe its leaves occasionally to remove dust and help the plant make better use of available light.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>9. Philodendron</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Philodendrons are popular indoor plants because they adapt well to indoor conditions. Their attractive foliage and preference for humid environments make them a good choice during the monsoon.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: Provide indirect sunlight, well-draining soil and avoid excessive watering.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>10. Lucky Bamboo</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Lucky Bamboo is a compact plant that can be grown in water, making it a convenient option for homes and offices. It prefers bright, indirect light and can add a decorative touch to indoor spaces.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Care tip: If growing it in water, change the water regularly and keep the container clean.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>How to Care for Indoor Plants During Monsoon</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Although humidity can benefit many plants, excessive moisture can create problems. Follow these simple monsoon indoor plant care tips:</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><ul><li>Avoid overwatering your plants.</li><li>Use pots with proper drainage holes.</li><li>Keep indoor plants where they receive sufficient indirect sunlight.</li><li>Ensure good air circulation around the plants.</li><li>Remove yellow or damaged leaves promptly.</li><li>Check regularly for fungus, mould and pests.</li><li>Do not allow excess water to remain in trays under the pots.</li><li>Reduce watering when the soil stays wet for several days.</li></ul></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><div><h2>Why Choose Indoor Plants During Monsoon?</h2></div></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>Indoor plants can make your home feel fresher and more inviting during the rainy season. Plants with attractive foliage can also add natural colour to rooms and brighten up indoor spaces when cloudy weather reduces outdoor light.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>However, every plant has different light and watering requirements. Before bringing a plant indoors, check whether your room provides the right conditions for its growth.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>The monsoon can be a good time to grow indoor plants because increased humidity supports several tropical and moisture-loving varieties. Snake Plant, Money Plant, Spider Plant, Peace Lily, Boston Fern, Areca Palm, ZZ Plant, Rubber Plant, Philodendron and Lucky Bamboo are some options to consider.</p></div></div></div><div class=\" \"><div class=\"undefined\"><div class=\"Content_Content__Bx4Rj\"><p>The key to healthy plants during the rainy season is proper drainage, controlled watering, adequate indirect light and good ventilation. With the right care, these plants can keep your indoor space green and fresh throughout the monsoon.</p></div></div></div><div class=\"\"><div style=\"visibility:visible\" class=\" adCaller_bggrayAd__q6bNq   atfAdContainer adCaller_atfAdContainer__GlF1_ adCaller_overflow-hidden__jLJZj\"><div id=\"Adunit_Google-As-preferred-Source-ad-desktop\" class=\" dfp  adCaller_adDiv__4uZgm adCaller_ads-50-h__TiRs9\" data-adunit=\"/21806551354/TN_English/Desktop/ROS/TN_English_Desk_ROS_800x50\" data-dimensions=\"[[800,50]]\" data-section=\"spotlight\" data-pagetype=\"article\" data-metainfoattr=\"indoorplantsformonsoon,bestindoorplants,monsoonplants,indoorplantcareduringmonsoon,lowmaintenanceindoorplants,plantsforhome,Spotlight,TimesNow\" data-msid=\"155983454\" data-category-string=\"spotlight\" data-utm_source=\"TNN\" data-utm_medium=\"paid\"></div></div><section class=\"LatestNewsWidget_LatestNewsWidget__9iGk3 undefined\"><h2 class=\"LatestNewsWidget_heading__CJeMy\"><a href=\"https://www.timesnownews.com/latest-news\">Latest News<!-- -->  <svg class=\"SvgIcon_icon-md__09S9E\"><use xlink:href=\"/nimg/assets/icons/svg/sprite-global.svg?version=4#rightArrowIconGrey\"></use></svg> <svg class=\"SvgIcon_icon-md__09S9E\"><use xlink:href=\"/nimg/assets/icons/svg/sprite-global.svg?version=4#rightArrowIconGrey\"></use></svg></a></h2><div><button class=\"LatestNewsWidget_customArrow__R09MT LatestNewsWidget_prevArrow__ahb_9\" disabled=\"\" aria-label=\"Previous\"></button><div class=\"slick-slider slick-initialized\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"slick-list\"><div class=\"slick-track\" style=\"width:320%;left:0%\"><div data-index=\"0\" class=\"slick-slide slick-active slick-current\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"false\" style=\"outline:none;width:12.5%\"><div><div class=\"LatestNewsWidget_NewsWidget__54FYk\" tabindex=\"-1\" style=\"width:100%;display:inline-block\"><div class=\"LatestNewsWidget_NewsWidgetImg__26U77\"><div><span><a href=\"https://www.timesnownews.com/technology-science\">technology science</a></span><h3><a href=\"https://www.timesnownews.com/technology-science/iphone-18-pro-max-18-pro-india-sale-starts-tomorrow-time-locations-offers-price-how-to-buy-one-in-your-city-article-156175574\">iPhone 18 Pro Max, 1